message: "If you use or reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Paradox of Origin: Formal Incompleteness, the Jevons Paradox, and the Structural Necessity of Human Judgment in AI Systems"
abstract: >
  This paper argues that artificial intelligence systems are structurally
  incapable of full cognitive autonomy, for reasons that are formal, empirical,
  economic, and interactional. Drawing on Gödel's incompleteness theorems,
  Model Collapse (Shumailov et al., 2024), the Jevons rebound effect,
  Truth Inflation, and AI sycophancy, it introduces the Paradox of Origin:
  the more technically capable an AI system becomes, the more it reveals
  its structural dependency on human judgment. The paper proposes the
  Verification Triad (human agent + generative AI + formal verifier) as a
  constructive architectural response. Co-authored by a human researcher
  and two AI systems as a performative instantiation of its central thesis.
